109:In this paper we shall focus on the existence of $3$-SCHGDDs of type $(n,m^t)$ with $t$ even. When $t$ is odd, the existence problem has been discussed in \cite{fwc} recently.
112:\begin{enumerate}
115:\end{enumerate}
124:We are to prove in Sections $3$ and $4$ that when $t$ is odd and $n\neq 8$ or $t$ is doubly even and $t\neq 8$, the existence problem for $3$-SCHGDDs is completely solved, and when $t$ is singly even, many infinite families are obtained.
126:Although the existence problem for SCHGDDs is interesting in its own right, there are actually some nice applications such as in the construction of two-dimensional balanced sampling plans and optimal two-dimensional optical orthogonal codes. We shall consider these applications in Section $5$. Actually, the  main result of this paper has been used for constructing optimal three dimensional optical orthogonal codes by Wang and Chang \cite{wlc}.
